// 63c CONTROL — a clause pair that is NOT a complement, and must be REFUSED.
//
// Without this file, `Complement` compiling proves nothing: a checker that
// accepts any two-clause function accepts complementary pairs too. This file
// differs from `Complement`'s `Gt` in exactly one character — `<=` becomes `>=`
// — so the two clauses overlap instead of partitioning, and every integer in
// 1..1000 is covered by neither.
//
// It must FAIL with an inexhaustiveness diagnostic naming the residual. If it
// compiles, 63c measured nothing and the `Complement` result is worthless.
module NotComplement

public atom Gt(int n)
Gt(n) when n > 1000 -> :yes
Gt(n) when n >= 1000 -> :no
